Z||000003||1FST2M6||05-08-2000||08:37 AM||||yes on this chart it was... but even when its off it will still peak at like 285lbft. the weight of the car shifting on the dyno, the hard shock of the solid unsprung clutch do wonders for this! no the headers are not on as of yet... they have their thermal protective barrier coating on them (not quite the same as ceramic coating) I've lost reverse and then 1st gear.. the bushings in the top of the tranny are shot.. i've ordered a tranny from Mike Valentine  (84 4spd.  w/4:10)  once i drop in the tranny I'll put the headers in then and run her on the dyno... more to follow soon... <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 05-08-2000).]||||reg||1
